    "body": "Add a config for [kconfig-lsp](https://github.com/cccheng/kconfig-lsp), a language server for Kconfig.\n\nKconfig is the configuration language of the Linux kernel. Zephyr, U-Boot, coreboot, Buildroot, ESP-IDF and other projects also use it. Neovim already detects these files as the `kconfig` filetype (`Kconfig`, `Kconfig.*`, `Config.in`).\n\nThe server provides:\n- hover, go to definition, references and rename for symbols\n- completion of keywords and symbols\n- diagnostics for parse errors, undefined symbols and type errors\n- document symbols, workspace symbols, folding ranges and document links for `source` paths\n\nInstall it with `cargo install kconfig-lsp`.\n\nThe config uses:\n- `cmd = { 'kconfig-lsp' }`\n- `filetypes = { 'kconfig' }`\n- `root_markers = { '.git', 'Kconfig' }`\n\nThe brief also shows how to turn on the Kconfig extensions of Zephyr with `init_options`.\n\n### Popularity\n\nThe repository has fewer than 100 stars, so this config does not meet the star criterion in CONTRIBUTING.md. Other evidence:\n- The crate is published on [crates.io](https://crates.io/crates/kconfig-lsp). It has had regular releases (current version 0.3.4) and the CI runs tests.\n- Kconfig has a large and active user base: every Linux kernel developer, and the Zephyr, U-Boot and coreboot communities.\n- No other Kconfig language server config exists in nvim-lspconfig.",
